<title>GERMANY: Major German companies move to cut sick pay.</title>
<headline>Major German companies move to cut sick pay.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major German companies, including Mannesmann AG, Bayerische Vereinsbank AG, Bayerische Hypo-Bank AG, Continental AG and Schering AG, said on Wednesday they would soon cut sick pay to 80 percent of normal pay, in line with a recent change in labour laws.</p>
<p>The companies, in response to queries by Reuters, said they saw no need to wait, despite warnings by senior government officials that the legal change does not apply to existing contracts.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
